# Store these byte-for-byte with CRLF rather than normalising to LF.
#
# `text eol=crlf` would convert on checkout but still store LF — and the
# Windows setup file is meant to be downloaded straight from GitHub, which
# serves what is stored. cmd.exe can mishandle labels and goto in a file with
# LF endings, so the bytes have to be right in the repository itself.
*.bat -text
*.ps1 -text

# Everything else stays LF, including the shell scripts.
*.sh  text eol=lf
